                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This adaptation of the gamebooks works well in my regard. The top-down view of the adventurer traveling through maps and mazes creates a feeling of \"being there\", a consistency in a lived-in world. I like the battle and skill system, although it might seem unbalanced; it's just fun rolling the dice and hoping against hope. The stories from the books are somewhat abridged, the logic does not always work out, but it was a fun romp nonetheless. Graphics are good (especially the monster cards) and the music is unobtrusively atmosperic.",
